==Dutch==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|nl|dum|suster}}, from {{inh|nl|odt|swester}}, from {{inh|nl|gem-pro|*swestēr}}, from {{inh|nl|ine-pro|*swésōr}}. The sense “nurse” developed around 1900 due to nuns' activity in institutional care, especially from the mid nineteenth century until the mid twentieth century.

